This modified implementation provides a Rust C2S parser, numerical judgement
calculation, direct CPU raster rendering, and a bounded HTTP worker service.
It is based on the standalone parser/calculation port in:
https://github.com/watagashi-uni/chuni-judgement
Original contributors' rights are retained.

Original judgement behaviour reference:
https://github.com/pingfanH/umiguri-re
Commit 3aa8ebc53030cd178d5d90201e4ae2036f61c0bd
The original numerical implementation followed cw() and judgeWindows.
The current ground-note protection instead follows independently recovered
static rules in chusanApp.exe: original pair-time midpoints, FIX lower bounds,
per-type MINIMALIZE, and complete EXT coverage. The analyzed binary SHA-256 is
77ad8c04046ac895fc777a5eb66e6c6f23bd5a6bbf1dbb11f7b2f64adaba1123.
This implements normal TAP/EXT and FLICK touch windows, not a complete game
input/state simulator. Attribution to the earlier reference is retained.
No game bundle, art, sound or upstream source file is redistributed here.
